WEBVTT

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:10.480
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:12.650
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:16.160
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.900
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:34.200
Mr. Penguin's Secret!

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:43.650
But, Polar Bear,

00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:45.990
if they invented a copy robot,

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:48.540
it could be drinking 
café mocha like this,

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:50.470
and you could be eating ramen 
at the same time.

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:53.020
If that's what 
it would be used for,

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:55.530
I don't think it really 
needs to be invented.

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:59.990
Oh, that's right. I was making pizza.

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:01.560
I think I'll take some.

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:06.420
I thought I'd make a character pizza.

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:09.480
Noguchi Hideo?

00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:11.320
It was rough.

00:02:11.870 --> 00:02:13.810
When you fold this pizza...

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:18.950
See? He looks like he's laughing.

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:24.170
That's not all. 
If you fold it the other way...

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:28.510
He looks sad, doesn't he?

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:32.220
I wonder if that ability is 
really needed for a pizza.

00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:33.930
Eat up.

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:37.040
He's not the kind of guy
 you put on a pizza.

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:41.080
Could I get another
 café mocha, Miss Sasako?

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:41.740
Sure.

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:46.400
I'm tired.

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:49.980
Here you go.

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:52.550
Welcome, Panda.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:54.520
Thanks.

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:57.890
Here, Panda, have some pizza.

00:02:57.890 --> 00:02:59.820
Nope. Don't want it.

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:01.880
You'll demand gratitude back forever.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:05.320
I'm not that petty.

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:07.950
Though I may demand some gratitude.

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:10.030
So you are going to demand some...

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:13.600
Actually, it's from Polar Bear.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:15.620
In that case, I'll have it.

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:17.520
So you did want it...

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:20.190
By the way, Polar Bear,

00:03:20.190 --> 00:03:23.560
I started the "long breath diet" recently.

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:25.070
Want to do it with me?

00:03:25.070 --> 00:03:27.890
I'm working right now, so could 
we talk about this later?

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:38.340
Miss Sasako, I thought of a good way of

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:41.330
getting more pocket tissue
 hand-outs than anyone else.

00:03:41.330 --> 00:03:43.960
Oh, could I get another 
café mocha, Polar Bear?

00:03:46.670 --> 00:03:48.210
But you know,

00:03:48.210 --> 00:03:50.910
isn't raw egg over rice delicious?

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:55.230
I could talk about its 
deliciousness all night.

00:03:56.480 --> 00:03:58.140
Oh, it's about time

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:00.450
for my ventriloquism classes, 
so I'm gonna take off.

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:02.330
See you later, Panda.

00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:03.250
Okay.

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:05.560
See you later.

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:08.020
Bye!

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:10.020
Thank you very much.

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:14.380
I wonder what's up 
with Mr. Penguin...

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:16.520
Huh? What do you mean?

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:20.720
Mr. Penguin is always 
at the café, talking, right?

00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:22.430
He is always here.

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:25.720
I wonder what he does 
when he's not here.

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:26.530
I'm not sure...

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:29.070
Does he not work?

00:04:29.070 --> 00:04:31.290
I always just thought 
he was unemployed.

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:35.210
But he comes to the café daily, 
and is always out having fun, right?

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:38.620
I wonder how he gets onto the chair...

00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:42.480
I wonder what kind of job he has...

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:44.830
Where does he live?

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:48.950
You probably shouldn't 
pry into it too much.

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:50.100
He's right.

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:54.830
Would a camera help?

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:57.640
So you are going to have 
him investigate...

00:04:58.120 --> 00:04:59.440
Well, I want to know, too.

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:01.030
All right!

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:06.120
Starting tomorrow, I'm going to expose 
everything about Mr. Penguin!

00:05:07.070 --> 00:05:09.540
I think you may be using 
the wrong word there.

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:14.250
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:20.670
So that's when I asked them,

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:23.200
"I don't get points for that?"

00:05:24.140 --> 00:05:25.630
And they said that I don't.

00:05:26.990 --> 00:05:28.730
I'm tired of talking.

00:05:28.730 --> 00:05:30.090
I think I'll head home.

00:05:34.170 --> 00:05:35.560
See you later.

00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:38.960
All right, here I go.

00:05:40.550 --> 00:05:41.720
Good luck.

00:05:42.590 --> 00:05:45.170
Be sure to find out 
some of his weaknesses.

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:48.610
I think your intention is gradually changing...

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:53.990
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:06:13.730 --> 00:06:14.660
This is hilarious!

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:18.310
Karaoke

00:06:18.530 --> 00:06:22.270
<i>To the lucky boys and girls that 
stumbled upon this café</i>

00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:25.810
<i>We welcome you with an amazing menu</i>

00:06:25.810 --> 00:06:27.350
<i>Oh, just for you...</i>

00:06:29.470 --> 00:06:31.490
Birdland

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:35.950
You're awesome, Mr. Penguin!

00:06:38.010 --> 00:06:40.790
You're awesome, Anteater!

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:48.540
So he's drinking with Anteater...

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:49.770
One more time, one more time!

00:06:49.310 --> 00:06:51.280
Excuse me... Mr. Panda...

00:06:49.770 --> 00:06:51.280
Oh, that's awesome!

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:52.850
One more time, one more time!

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:54.550
You're sort of in the way.

00:06:54.550 --> 00:06:55.760
That's awesome!

00:06:55.760 --> 00:06:57.790
Hey, Pops, can we get 
some mozuku seaweed?

00:06:57.790 --> 00:06:59.390
You sure you don't want any ants?

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:02.860
An't nothing bad when you're drunk!

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:06.870
That was great, Anteater! 
You got that right!

00:07:06.870 --> 00:07:08.820
You can't just eat 
ants all the time...

00:07:09.410 --> 00:07:13.320
So Anteater can eat anything 
when he's drunk.

00:07:14.150 --> 00:07:16.040
Um, Mr. Panda...

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:19.070
He's cute, so I guess it's okay.

00:07:23.590 --> 00:07:25.280
So...

00:07:23.590 --> 00:07:25.280
Sloth?

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:28.960
Why'd you write that with a pen?

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:31.030
Come on, it won't come off, then.

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:35.650
Apparently he can speak 
faster in his sleep...

00:07:36.910 --> 00:07:38.180
Thanks!

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:40.290
Thanks for coming!

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:42.280
Two drafts!

00:07:42.280 --> 00:07:43.540
Yes, coming right up!

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:49.690
Birdland

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:54.300
So, you ended up losing him.

00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:55.130
Yeah.

00:07:56.570 --> 00:07:58.950
Maybe we should have him eat these.

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:02.760
I snuck a GPS transmitter in them.

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:06.250
I don't think you need 
to go that far...

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:10.980
But I did find out that he 
lazes around and has fun.

00:08:10.980 --> 00:08:13.930
That's something we could 
have found out here.

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:18.980
But apparently Mr. Anteater can 
eat anything when he's drunk.

00:08:18.980 --> 00:08:23.520
I was surprised that Sloth could 
talk faster in his sleep, too.

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:24.630
Indeed.

00:08:24.630 --> 00:08:27.910
Those both are far better 
than Mr. Penguin's secrets.

00:08:30.210 --> 00:08:33.350
I borrowed this from Rin Rin.

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:35.930
A video camera?

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:39.280
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:08:39.760 --> 00:08:42.780
I'm going to record Mr. Penguin

00:08:42.780 --> 00:08:45.120
getting on a chair on video today.

00:08:46.310 --> 00:08:48.430
He's always already on the chair,

00:08:48.430 --> 00:08:50.950
so I don't know how he gets on.

00:08:51.460 --> 00:08:54.560
So today, let's finally 
see how he does it.

00:08:56.410 --> 00:08:57.240
Welcome.

00:08:57.650 --> 00:09:01.150
Man, it sure smells 
like spring already.

00:09:01.150 --> 00:09:03.360
I ran into Mr. Llama over there.

00:09:03.360 --> 00:09:04.380
Hello.

00:09:04.380 --> 00:09:05.560
Oh, he's here.

00:09:06.830 --> 00:09:09.480
Did you want another serving 
of bamboo grass, Panda?

00:09:11.260 --> 00:09:12.840
I do!

00:09:14.260 --> 00:09:16.010
I'll have a café mocha.

00:09:16.010 --> 00:09:17.330
And could I get a coffee?

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:20.510
And just like that, 
he's already sitting again...

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:26.420
But it's on video,
 so that's not a problem.

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:34.800
All right, let's watch.

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:38.600
Man, it sure smells 
like spring already.

00:09:38.860 --> 00:09:41.050
I ran into Mr. Llama over there.

00:09:41.050 --> 00:09:42.070
Hello.

00:09:42.070 --> 00:09:43.160
Oh, he's here.

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:45.020
Here it comes...

00:09:47.270 --> 00:09:48.230
Hey.

00:09:49.820 --> 00:09:51.330
We can't see him.

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:00.850
So that's how Mr. Llama 
gets onto a chair.

00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:02.320
It seems so...

00:10:03.630 --> 00:10:07.810
But we didn't find out 
anything about Mr. Penguin.

00:10:10.120 --> 00:10:11.000
Oh!

00:10:11.760 --> 00:10:13.130
What is it?

00:10:13.850 --> 00:10:14.870
His wallet.

00:10:15.320 --> 00:10:18.250
All right, I think I'll head home now.

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:20.050
You're right.

00:10:20.530 --> 00:10:22.320
See you guys later!

00:10:27.830 --> 00:10:30.710
So he carries it under his flipper.

00:10:30.710 --> 00:10:32.330
It appears so.

00:10:32.810 --> 00:10:36.700
Speaking of which, I think he mentioned 
buying a wallet recently.

00:10:37.660 --> 00:10:38.990
Either way,

00:10:39.630 --> 00:10:42.550
it was a secret we didn't 
really need to know about.

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:53.960
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:58.880
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:10:55.310 --> 00:10:57.130
Cherry Blossom Viewing in Spring.

00:10:58.880 --> 00:11:01.340
Comfortable 
Housing

00:11:00.620 --> 00:11:01.340
Oh?

00:11:01.770 --> 00:11:04.600
Are you going to buy a 
house, Mr. Penguin?

00:11:05.020 --> 00:11:07.010
I'm thinking about moving.

00:11:07.950 --> 00:11:09.350
You're moving?

00:11:11.010 --> 00:11:13.730
The lease on my apartment
 runs out soon,

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:16.350
so I'm thinking about 
moving altogether.

00:11:16.660 --> 00:11:20.530
So you live in an 
apartment, Mr. Penguin?

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:22.990
I do. Didn't I tell you?

00:11:23.340 --> 00:11:27.750
Isn't it hard going to a real estate 
agent when you're a penguin?

00:11:28.030 --> 00:11:29.030
No, it's not.

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:38.620
So, I guess Mr. Penguin is moving...

00:11:39.030 --> 00:11:39.790
Yes.

00:11:40.560 --> 00:11:44.580
It'll be lonely, but I guess 
it is the season of goodbyes.

00:11:59.060 --> 00:12:01.240
Could you pick out 
some flowers for me?

00:12:01.720 --> 00:12:03.490
What kind of flowers 
are you looking for?

00:12:03.840 --> 00:12:04.700
Let's see...

00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:15.690
Oh, Mr. Polar Bear.

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:22.010
Ms. Donkey finally let me bake 
some baguettes for the first time.

00:12:22.950 --> 00:12:24.300
Please have some.

00:12:26.440 --> 00:12:27.520
Thanks.

00:12:36.650 --> 00:12:37.760
It's delicious.

00:12:38.120 --> 00:12:39.020
Yeah.

00:12:40.370 --> 00:12:42.870
Oh yeah, Penguin stopped 
in the other day.

00:12:45.300 --> 00:12:47.590
He said something about moving.

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:53.990
Well, it's spring.

00:12:58.460 --> 00:12:59.280
Yeah.

00:13:15.030 --> 00:13:17.870
How about this, Miss Sasako?

00:13:17.870 --> 00:13:18.860
What is it?

00:13:18.860 --> 00:13:22.440
Polar 
Bear 
Zeki

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:22.080
The Ryogoku Kokugikan.

00:13:23.340 --> 00:13:25.770
I made it with sweetfish candy.

00:13:27.890 --> 00:13:31.940
There seems to be something resembling 
a shachihoko sticking out...

00:13:34.280 --> 00:13:35.020
Huh?

00:13:39.390 --> 00:13:41.140
The café mocha recipe?

00:13:43.230 --> 00:13:44.440
Did you write this

00:13:45.190 --> 00:13:47.180
for Mr. Penguin?

00:13:48.940 --> 00:13:50.500
That's not it.

00:13:58.390 --> 00:13:59.640
Hey.

00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:03.650
Polar 
Bear 
Zeki

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:02.820
What is this?

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:03.970
The Kokugikan?

00:14:04.290 --> 00:14:07.860
You really are something, Polar Bear.

00:14:07.860 --> 00:14:09.530
Go ahead, dig in.

00:14:10.350 --> 00:14:12.580
Also... here...

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:16.540
You know, if you ever 
want to drink it...

00:14:17.470 --> 00:14:21.280
Oh, that's right. I renewed my lease.

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:22.500
Eh?

00:14:23.120 --> 00:14:25.900
So you're not moving?

00:14:25.900 --> 00:14:28.610
It's too troublesome to 
find another place.

00:14:33.200 --> 00:14:34.180
I see.

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:40.100
That's great, isn't it,
 Mr. Polar Bear?

00:14:42.810 --> 00:14:43.860
I guess.

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:46.280
What?

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:47.630
What happened?

00:14:47.630 --> 00:14:49.030
It's nothing.

00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:51.310
I totally want to know now.

00:14:51.310 --> 00:14:56.580
Oh, did you discover the best time
 to spit out gum after it loses its flavor?

00:14:56.920 --> 00:14:57.850
Nope.

00:14:59.050 --> 00:15:02.260
Come on, Polar Bear, tell me.

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:06.260
What's that piece of paper?

00:15:08.520 --> 00:15:10.220
It's nothing.

00:15:12.370 --> 00:15:14.390
All right. Let's do it.

00:15:15.440 --> 00:15:16.690
Do what?

00:15:18.720 --> 00:15:19.820
Cherry blossom viewing.

00:15:25.810 --> 00:15:28.130
The cherry blossoms are amazing.

00:15:28.530 --> 00:15:30.180
They're beautiful.

00:15:31.590 --> 00:15:33.810
They bloomed beautifully 
this year, too.

00:15:34.560 --> 00:15:36.690
Though I think I say that every year.

00:15:37.150 --> 00:15:39.330
That's because they're 
beautiful every year.

00:15:41.300 --> 00:15:43.030
It sure goes by fast...

00:15:43.490 --> 00:15:46.340
It's already been a year

00:15:46.340 --> 00:15:48.520
since we met Panda and Miss Sasako.

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:54.430
Indeed. It's already been a year...

00:15:55.730 --> 00:16:00.700
We saw many different sides 
of Mr. Penguin this year.

00:16:10.600 --> 00:16:13.990
Could you remember something 
a little better than that?

00:16:14.410 --> 00:16:15.830
Hey!

00:16:17.550 --> 00:16:20.210
We're gonna drink! 
It's cherry blossom viewing time!

00:16:20.700 --> 00:16:22.580
Fire it up, fire it up!

00:16:23.030 --> 00:16:25.500
Welcome, Grizzly.

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:27.840
All right! Let's drink today!

00:16:28.450 --> 00:16:31.770
All right! I'm gonna eat 
bamboo grass today!

00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:35.510
You eat that all year 'round...

00:16:36.140 --> 00:16:38.500
The cherry blossoms are magnificent.

00:16:38.990 --> 00:16:44.850
I bought... drinks...

00:16:45.510 --> 00:16:49.280
Thanks. All right, 
everyone have a seat.

00:16:50.720 --> 00:16:52.440
Hello, Mr. Handa.

00:16:53.010 --> 00:16:56.440
Thank you for the mandarins 
the other day.

00:16:57.380 --> 00:16:59.350
No problem at all. This is...

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:01.760
Oh, nice to meet you.

00:17:01.760 --> 00:17:04.250
My name is Kirino and 
I work under Mr. Handa.

00:17:04.600 --> 00:17:07.710
This is my first time coming 
to Polar Bear's Café.

00:17:08.110 --> 00:17:09.340
I see.

00:17:09.810 --> 00:17:11.960
Please come visit.

00:17:12.310 --> 00:17:14.930
Oh, I will! Definitely!

00:17:14.930 --> 00:17:16.610
Thank you.

00:17:16.610 --> 00:17:19.430
I'll make sure I stop by often.

00:17:19.430 --> 00:17:22.120
Really? Thank you.

00:17:23.260 --> 00:17:26.190
I-I think once in a while 
would be better...

00:17:26.590 --> 00:17:27.980
Rarely would be even better...

00:17:29.250 --> 00:17:32.470
Come on, Masaki, get a move on.

00:17:32.470 --> 00:17:34.570
The coffee's gonna get cold.

00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:36.070
I know!

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:37.990
Please have some.

00:17:38.480 --> 00:17:41.240
This is special coffee 
that Master and I made.

00:17:41.820 --> 00:17:44.040
All right, let's all have some.

00:17:44.690 --> 00:17:46.430
Panda!

00:17:46.870 --> 00:17:48.000
Hey!

00:17:56.470 --> 00:17:58.390
Mr. Full-Time Panda!

00:18:04.840 --> 00:18:07.680
It's been a while, Panda.

00:18:10.210 --> 00:18:11.080
Yeah!

00:18:12.580 --> 00:18:16.170
Did you get fired from your new zoo?

00:18:17.300 --> 00:18:18.500
No...

00:18:19.170 --> 00:18:21.320
I took some time off.

00:18:22.130 --> 00:18:24.070
I wanted to see you, Panda.

00:18:25.340 --> 00:18:27.620
I'll be back here for a week.

00:18:28.630 --> 00:18:31.670
Aw, you should stay longer.

00:18:32.970 --> 00:18:33.770
Huh?

00:18:34.270 --> 00:18:35.380
What's the matter?

00:18:36.320 --> 00:18:38.720
You went to Singapore,

00:18:38.720 --> 00:18:40.620
but you didn't tan at all.

00:18:42.360 --> 00:18:45.720
Well... it is fur, you know...

00:18:55.860 --> 00:18:57.740
Here you go, Rin Rin.

00:18:58.150 --> 00:19:00.290
Oh, thank you very much.

00:19:02.350 --> 00:19:04.020
<i>I can die happy.</i>

00:19:04.020 --> 00:19:05.760
<i>I'm surrounded by pandas.</i>

00:19:07.980 --> 00:19:11.130
But, actually, Mr. Handa is here.

00:19:11.520 --> 00:19:12.280
Pardon?

00:19:13.310 --> 00:19:15.380
Totally unexpected.

00:19:17.860 --> 00:19:19.340
Prince Han!

00:19:20.250 --> 00:19:22.670
Wh-What is it, Mei Mei?

00:19:24.280 --> 00:19:28.520
Is it okay if I look at you, 
instead of the flowers?

00:19:29.670 --> 00:19:32.300
Oh my gosh, I said it!

00:19:34.440 --> 00:19:36.350
Handa... over flowers.

00:19:37.350 --> 00:19:39.600
Anyone want any penguin cards?

00:19:39.600 --> 00:19:42.500
Anyone want any penguin cards 
to go with flower viewing?

00:19:43.470 --> 00:19:45.090
They ain't sellin', so I'm drinkin'.

00:19:46.480 --> 00:19:48.540
Aren't the cherry blossoms beautiful?

00:19:49.460 --> 00:19:51.540
Close, close, way too close...

00:19:52.690 --> 00:19:55.810
Am I really that dull?

00:19:58.650 --> 00:19:59.520
Let's drink!

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:00.680
Well, thank you...

00:20:01.040 --> 00:20:06.850
I'll keep you company... for years...

00:20:07.700 --> 00:20:08.730
Mr. Penguin.

00:20:11.420 --> 00:20:13.470
It's been a while, Miss Penko.

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:15.780
I'm Penmi!

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:17.500
I'm sorry...

00:20:18.690 --> 00:20:21.800
Oh, that's right, today...

00:20:23.530 --> 00:20:25.750
We brought our little sisters.

00:20:27.750 --> 00:20:28.790
I'm Pen'eh.

00:20:29.930 --> 00:20:31.030
I'm Penne.

00:20:32.150 --> 00:20:33.290
I'm Penho.

00:20:34.330 --> 00:20:35.560
I'm Penyo.

00:20:36.490 --> 00:20:37.460
I'm Penyu.

00:20:38.180 --> 00:20:39.420
I'm Pentleen.

00:20:40.230 --> 00:20:42.010
I'm Pentrisha.

00:20:42.930 --> 00:20:45.530
Nice to meet you, Mr. Penguin.

00:20:46.980 --> 00:20:49.260
N-Nice to meet you...

00:20:49.260 --> 00:20:52.020
Um...

00:20:52.790 --> 00:20:54.930
I leave the rest to you, Mr. Llama!

00:20:56.010 --> 00:20:56.810
Hey!

00:20:56.810 --> 00:20:57.800
Wait!

00:20:57.800 --> 00:20:59.070
Mr. Penguin?

00:21:00.190 --> 00:21:03.580
It's been a while, 
Miss Penna and Miss Pennuelle.

00:21:03.580 --> 00:21:04.730
Indeed.

00:21:17.450 --> 00:21:19.400
There's even more people now.

00:21:19.790 --> 00:21:21.600
I wonder if we have enough drinks.

00:21:21.890 --> 00:21:23.920
Hey, you guys!

00:21:24.650 --> 00:21:26.360
What the hell are you doin'?

00:21:26.360 --> 00:21:27.890
Hurry and get over here!

00:21:29.830 --> 00:21:30.820
Let's go.

00:21:32.740 --> 00:21:33.480
Yeah!

00:21:34.400 --> 00:21:35.210
Let's.

00:21:35.880 --> 00:21:36.990
Indeed.

00:23:25.330 --> 00:23:26.920
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:23:26.920 --> 00:23:28.090
What it is, Panda?

00:23:28.090 --> 00:23:28.590
Let's end this.

00:23:28.590 --> 00:23:29.510
Too soon!

00:23:29.510 --> 00:23:30.680
Let's keep talking forever.

00:23:30.680 --> 00:23:31.640
Too long!

00:23:31.640 --> 00:23:35.390
Mr. Penguin, please tell 
the children of the world

00:23:35.390 --> 00:23:36.570
something wise.

00:23:36.570 --> 00:23:38.190
You should get used to drinking

00:23:38.190 --> 00:23:40.520
for whenever you going 
to split the bill.

00:23:40.520 --> 00:23:44.290
I don't think there's ever been 
something so useless to tell children.

00:23:44.290 --> 00:23:45.900
Let's end this, Mr. Polar Bear.

00:23:45.900 --> 00:23:47.370
Next week at this time,

00:23:47.370 --> 00:23:48.980
will be Polar Bear's Café episode 1.

00:23:48.980 --> 00:23:49.950
No, it won't.

00:23:49.950 --> 00:23:50.830
Let's end this.

00:23:51.310 --> 00:23:52.950
See you again!
